 "note": "Enforcement control plane (design section 10.5). Exact tracked paths. Every file under a deny_by_default_tree is control plane; a new or renamed one must be registered here in the same change (listing records membership, it never removes it). Paths outside those trees are listed because an in-plane driver reads them as policy, or because they are governance documents. Content a driver merely generates from (docs/manual-prose.json, docs/manual/**) is NOT in the plane. Policy paths a driver already names but that are not yet tracked (docs/capabilities.json, Tests/capability-tests.json) must be registered here, with a CODEOWNERS pattern, in the commit that adds them. No runtime loader consumes this file yet; Tests/automation/test_control_plane.py is its only checker. Deliberately excluded: Package.swift and Package.resolved (design section 10.5 classes them as governed execution surfaces checked by a trusted base diff, not policy implementations; a floor or dependency change is a dedicated PR under that check) and .gitignore (no in-plane driver reads it; its by-class leak patterns are governed by review). The manifest and CODEOWNERS are themselves in the plane.",
